// Contracts known to hold non-zero unshielded token balances on this environment's
// chain, for the unshieldedBalances regression tests (midnightntwrk/midnight-indexer#1245,
// getTokenHoldingContracts). Generated by qa/tools/block-scanner: contract addresses
// discovered in the block scan and not yet listed here are queried via contractAction,
// most recently active first, and up to 5 of them with a positive balance are appended
// per run. Existing entries, including hand-written ones and their comments, are never
// removed or rewritten. The token type is the contract's largest custom (non-NIGHT)
// balance, or its NIGHT balance when it holds no custom token.
//
// Balances are point-in-time: a contract can spend its tokens after the scan.
//
// The balances are read from the indexer, so the scanned indexer must carry the #1246
// fix and repaired history (backfill or reindex). When no new holder is found the file
// is left untouched, since an empty result cannot be told apart from the #1245 regression.
//
// NOTE: contract addresses do NOT survive a chain reset, and the scanner never removes
// entries. When a reset makes this file stale, delete it and re-run the scanner
// (bun run generate:data) to rebuild it.
[]
